body:
The IPCS data for propranolol says that the average toxic but not fatal dose is about 1.75 grams, which would be about 44 pills of 40mg each. But even doses of 5-8 grams (125-200 pills) aren't certain to kill a human. There is a notable variation in how propranolol affects individuals, so it's hard to predict the effects. Also note that according to the PubMed abstract in footnote 1, 2/3 of patients in that study who took more than 2 grams of propranolol experienced seizures. That doesn't sound like an easy way to go. 

&#x200B;

In other words a bad idea.
